B] Buffer cache:
            - stores data blocks read from disk
            - Largest memory area of SGA
            - Maintained with complex algorithm (LRU MOST recently used)
            - Reading block from disk handled by server process
            - changed blocks by DML called dirty blocks
            - stores index data too

c] Redo Log Buffer:
      - Handles data loss
      - Redo log rentry created when insert,update, delete, create, alter drop occurs
      - Redo log entries has the changes made to the database
      - They are used for recovery operations
      - redo log entries stored in redo log buffer
      - LGWR --> every three seconds, when it full, commmit
      - Circular buffer
      - rollback is not done with redo log data


